// REJECTS: Unexpected token '['. Valid alternatives: ['projects']
//
// Associations do NOT take a constraint block. A Class accepts '[' after its name; an
// Association accepts exactly one thing there, `projects`, and nothing else.
//
// Class and Association are near-identical in every other respect -- same body, same
// property syntax, same stereotype prefix, and DomainParseTreeWalker shares the property
// visitor between them. That similarity is the trap: a rewrite that factors "named element
// with an optional constraint list and a brace body" into one routine accepts constraints
// on an association, and the protocol has nowhere to put them.
###Pure
Association fixture::neg::ConstrainedAssoc
[
   c1: true
]
{
   parts: fixture::neg::Part[*];
   assembly: fixture::neg::Assembly[1];
}
